{"id":"crossbow","slug":"crossbow","name":"Crossbow","aliases":["Bowgun","Balister","Cross-bow","Crossbows","Cross bow","Cranequin","Cross-bows","Crannequin","Arbaletiers","Medieval european crossbow"],"kind":"firearm","category":"historical","subcategory":"Bow-like ranged weapon","description":"A crossbow is a ranged weapon using an elastic launching device consisting of a bow-like assembly called a prod, mounted horizontally on a main frame called a tiller, which is hand-held in a similar fashion to the stock of a long gun. Crossbows shoot arrow-like projectiles called bolts or quarrels. A person who shoots crossbow is called a crossbowman, an arbalister or an arbalist.","development":"A crossbow is essentially a bow mounted on an elongated frame (called a tiller or stock) with a built-in mechanism that holds the drawn bow string, as well as a trigger mechanism, which is used to release the string.","facts":[],"specifications":[],"specIndex":{},"images":{"hero":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Une_arbal%C3%A8te_classique.jpg/3840px-Une_arbal%C3%A8te_classique.jpg","width":4324,"height":2905,"license":"See Wikimedia Commons"},"thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Une_arbal%C3%A8te_classique.jpg/330px-Une_arbal%C3%A8te_classique.jpg"},"gallery":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/Crossbow_pistol_IMG_3841.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crossbow_pistol_IMG_3841.jpg","width":5616,"height":3744,"caption":"The Vaudois armory in the 19th century: Pistol crossbow for home recreational shooting. Made by Frédéric Siber in Morges, early 19th century. On display at Morges military museum, accession number 295.","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0 fr","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/fr/deed.en","attribution":"Rama"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ab/HJRK_A_108_-_Wallarmbrust_c._1460-70.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://co